    "body": "fix on issue/1051-planning-budget-edge · PR #1138 · pinned by adaptive::budget::tests::each_margin_attempt_is_held_to_the_budget_on_its_own, adaptive::budget::twins::the_r7_bars_levels_decide_the_same_way_under_sub_micron_perturbations, adaptive::budget::twins::the_windows_levels_decide_the_same_way_under_sub_micron_perturbations (heavy), and the two rotary_adaptive pins now naming the levels · merges when reviewed\n\nFinding: the edge was not the limits but the sum over margin attempts - a first attempt that ran out of wall margin (a matter of nanometres at ~140 revolutions) charged 22.5 k r to the retry, which was then refused 7.6 k r in. Held per attempt, the r7 bar's level 5.0 and the window's 6.0 / 5.0 are HSM-planned at 0, 8, 16, 62 and 250 nm alike. Stacked on #1080. Left open: which margin the plan is made from still turns on nanometres (different plans, same verdict); the first-margin plan of level 5.0 posts 5 breaks of 5.0-6.2 deg (#1050), the wider-margin one none.",
